Mage tank=
The passive effect of the [[confliction gauntlets]] combined with the fast attack speed of the [[Eye of Ayak]] results in reasonable DPS against monsters in the Inferno, even when wearing tanky melee armour that would normally render Magic attacks inaccurate. The benefit of this loadout compared to more conventional ranged methods is the increased melee and ranged defence provided by melee armour, which acts as a safety net in the event the player is hit off-prayer.
* It is recommended to aim for +60 Magic attack bonus while wearing tank gear; accuracy lower than this results in damage becoming too inconsistent against blobs.
* A [[Tumeken's shadow]] for magers, Jads, and Zuk is recommended to save on inventory space compared to bringing a ranged switch. Bringing a reasonable ranged switch in place of a shadow (e.g. Bow of Faerdhinen, crystal armour, necklace of anguish, Ava's assembler/Dizana's quiver, toxic blowpipe) will result in having to sacrifice supplies.
